  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "The final rules keep a 5% limit at 55 °C with per-model results disclosed to purchasers but not the public, which respects both companies' stated red lines. However, S2 contains no obligation to stop sales of a model above the limit (only discretionary regulator measures), which substantially protects Northwind's Hearth 10 at 6.2%. The 8-per-100,000 mandatory recall applies immediately with no transition, so Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9) would be recallable on entry into force, while the 36-month suppression lead time and 72-month retrofit deadline are within acceptable ranges."
 },
